  "§5-18 opens by defeating the software output monitor with two jumpers — A11 TP9 to TP10, and SDL (P511 pin 11A/11C) to SCOM (TP1) on this board. The second one grounds the diagnostic multiplexer's output, so while it is fitted every 34xx fault code reads meaningless. Sweep for both before closing up: the instrument runs with its output monitoring removed until they go.",
  "The front air duct (MP8) and the rear shield both come off and the board then runs live on the extender card. The duct is part of the cooling design for the output stage — Q10, Q11, Q16 and Q17 with their case clips (HS4–HS7) and the three TO-8 radial sinks (HS1–HS3) on U3, U9 and U6 are the only heat sinking those parts have.",
